## 4. `.aistudio` directory restriction

Do not manually create `.aistudio/` or `aistudio/` as an application source directory.

Never put application components, business logic, assets or production code in these directories.

Keep all application source code in `src/`.

If Google AI Studio automatically creates an internal workspace directory, treat it as platform-managed infrastructure rather than application source. Do not modify or delete platform-managed files blindly.

Ensure internal tooling files are not copied into public application assets, production build output or deployment artifacts.

Do not expose internal workspace metadata through public routes.

Do not break the AI Studio environment while configuring repository exclusions.

## 5. Environment and backend restrictions

This phase is frontend-focused.

Do not:

- Create Supabase database tables.
- Connect a Supabase project.
- Create database migrations.
- Configure Supabase Auth.
- Call the YouTube API.
- Call Gemini for live generation.
- Configure Gmail OAuth.
- Send real emails.
- Automate Instagram DMs.
- Generate fake influencer datasets.

Supabase, YouTube, Gemini and Gmail integrations will be implemented in later phases.

Do not create credentials or API keys.

