# PART 7 — RESPONSIVE DESIGN

Desktop is the primary reference, but the design must work on every common screen size.

### Large desktop: 1440px and above
- Centered content.
- Maximum width of 1200px.
- Full navigation.
- Two-column product showcases.
- Full-width dark audience section.
- Horizontal workflow.

### Standard desktop: 1024–1439px
- Maintain balanced content width.
- Reduce section padding where appropriate.
- Preserve readable product mockups.
- Prevent text and dashboard overlap.

### Tablet: 768–1023px
- Adapt two-column layouts.
- Allow workflow steps to wrap.
- Maintain readable headings.
- Keep navigation usable.

### Mobile: below 768px
- Mobile navigation.
- Stack hero content.
- Scale dashboard previews carefully.
- Convert horizontal feature tabs into a horizontally scrollable tab row or suitable stacked controls.
- Stack all alternating feature sections.
- Stack the audience comparison.
- Convert the workflow into a vertical timeline.
- Ensure CTA buttons are easy to tap.
- Avoid horizontal page overflow.

All text, product preview elements, tables and controls must remain legible.

